-   when the store is performed.  This should be sufficient to implement
-   the architecturally mandated semantics, and avoids having to monitor
-   regular stores.  The compare vs the remembered value is done during
-   the cmpxchg operation, but we must compare the addresses manually.  */
+   the value/address loaded, and comparing the address when the store
+   is performed.  Regular stores are not monitored.  When no other vCPU
+   or thread can write memory, the store succeeds whenever the address
+   matches, so a regular store by the same CPU does not clear the local
+   monitor (IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED).  Otherwise the cmpxchg also checks
+   that memory still holds the value loaded, in place of a global
